I&#x27;ve been enjoying worktree managers like vibe-kanban and quickly realized I cannot run multiple dev servers, which is a huge no for me. Changing ports for each branch kinda works, but isn&#x27;t the most efficient way.<p>Turns out 127.0.0.0&#x2F;8 gives 16M loopback IPs and they&#x27;re being wasted, so I decided to put them to work and change IPs instead of ports :3 the usage is quite simple<p><pre><code>  silo &lt;whatever&gt;
</code></pre>
then each worktree&#x2F;branch gets a deterministic IP, so you don&#x27;t have to think about it.<p>it&#x27;s not 100% functional (and full of unsafe lol) but wanted to share this first
